   "subject": "accelerated failure time (AT) models on nimble",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"#0563C1\" vlink=\"#954F72\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Hi All<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">I am wondering if there is a simpler way to fit AFT survival models on Nimble. Currently we have converted\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">BUGS code that uses a zeroes trick for an arbitrary likelihood.\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">I assume that we would have to do this on nimble also.<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">OpenBUGS had a\r\n</span></font><font size=\"3\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">dloglik generic function\r\n</span></font>which implements  a zeroes trick <font size=\"3\" face=\"Courier New\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Does anyone know of a (more) efficient way to do this on Nimble ?<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Best<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Andrew Lawson<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"#1f497d\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "8LrelHo2AwAJ",
   "from": "Chris Paciorek",
