   "date": "2023-07-06T21:12:48Z",
   "subject": "Re: accelerated failure time (AT) models on nimble",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Andrew,<div><br></div><div>Instead of the zeroes trick, we generally suggest users write a <a href=\"https://r-nimble.org/html_manual/cha-user-defined.html#sec:user-distributions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://r-nimble.org/html_manual/cha-user-defined.html%23sec:user-distributions&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792476102406000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Y9fT6p41VSFxl57l_QLMd\">user-defined distribution</a> to implement the likelihood of interest.</div><div>So at a high level, that is what I suggest here.</div><div><br></div><div>-chris</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thu, Jul 6, 2023 at 10:55 AM Lawson, Andrew B. &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">laws...@musc.edu</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\">Hi All<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\">I am wondering if there is a simpler way to fit AFT survival models on Nimble. Currently we have converted\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\">BUGS code that uses a zeroes trick for an arbitrary likelihood.\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\">I assume that we would have to do this on nimble also.<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\">OpenBUGS had a\r\n</span></font><font size=\"3\" face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">dloglik generic function\r\n</span></font>which implements  a zeroes trick <font size=\"3\" face=\"Courier New\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\">Does anyone know of a (more) efficient way to do this on Nimble ?<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\">Best<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\">Andrew Lawson<u></u><u></u></span></font></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" color=\"#1f497d\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></font></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p></p></div></blockquote></div>"
